Package: 1bit-engine
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: 1bit <packages@1bit.gg>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.39), libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, libgomp1, libpcre2-8-0
Description: the 1bit engine and the server it runs models with
 1bit OS, Lemonade Server appliance: the engine binary, the HRX
 llama-server and its libraries, the ds4 programs, the sealed NPU
 kernel sets and the two commands that prove a boot (1bit-selftest,
 1bit-release-check). Installed under /opt/1bit, which is where the
 engine looks once its build tree is gone.
 .
 The engine's own libraries are found beside it ($ORIGIN). The ROCm
 userspace (HIP, rocBLAS, hipBLASLt, the HSA runtime) is the
 machine's, not this package's: upstream ours came from the SDK the
 build machine had, and on a box it has to come from packages
 (see os/v2/README.md, "The ROCm userspace").
